/E (    Cognitive biases are predictable patterns of deviation from rationality in judgment. Examples include confirmation bias \(seeking information that confirms existing beliefs\), availability bias \(overweighting easily recalled information\), and sunk cost fallacy \(continuing investments because of past costs\). Awareness of biases enables compensatory strategies.)
